{"answerText":"Submit a **Post Approval Amendment (PAA)** in DOB NOW to revise an approved filing’s scope or drawings. Because this filing was not submitted as a legalization, do **not** select Legalization for the revision; the DOB NOW guide says legalization filings result in a no-work permit and PAAs are unavailable after Legalization is selected.

Disclose the approved work being revised and clearly describe every change to the approved scope and drawings. The supplied guidance does not establish a numeric cap or other general substantive limit on the extent of a PAA revision.

This conclusion is based on noncontrolling DOB NOW guidance, not on the supplied 2022 Building Code passages. Those enacted passages address specialized drawing content (such as temporary structures, formwork, and structural details), not DOB NOW filing-action selection or PAA limits.","supportedPoints":[{"heading":"The supplied Building Code does not establish the DOB NOW revision action","explanation":"The assembled 2022 NYC Building Code provisions prescribe drawing content only for particular subjects, including architectural construction documents, temporary structures or installations, formwork, joists and decking, and trusses. They do not establish whether an approved DOB NOW filing must be revised through a PAA, whether Legalization may be selected, or a general limit on the revision’s scope.","sectionID":"48","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:48-10","research-permitext_discovered-id:52-7","research-permitext_discovered-id:3654-2","research-permitext_discovered-id:3659-1","research-permitext_discovered-id:6125-8","research-permitext_discovered-id:6199-4","research-permitext_discovered-id:4818-3","research-permitext_discovered-id:4880-6"]}],"assumptions":[],"missingFacts":[],"followUpQuestions":[],"evidenceLimitations":["The supplied enacted evidence is limited to selected 2022 NYC Building Code drawing and temporary-construction provisions; it contains no enacted DOB NOW PAA or Legalization workflow rule. The filing-action conclusion therefore relies only on the supplied noncontrolling official DOB guidance.","The supplied DOB NOW guidance establishes the PAA mechanism, the Legalization/PAA limitation, and the need to identify and describe revisions, but does not establish a broader numeric or substantive cap on revisions."],"additionalEvidenceNeeded":["If an enacted or binding administrative basis is needed for the PAA workflow or any limits on revision scope, provide the applicable NYC Administrative Code, DOB rule, or DOB NOW filing instruction that governs this filing type."],"supportingSourceUses":[{"sourceID":"web-source-eff9cc5f5b0cfde883cce536","claimID":"web-claim-d07e8335774d526021e7e0c8"},{"sourceID":"web-source-eff9cc5f5b0cfde883cce536","claimID":"web-claim-a764a91149559757f6d17c33"},{"sourceID":"web-source-eff9cc5f5b0cfde883cce536","claimID":"web-claim-8db8a02f7983a28c6ae635f9"}],"citations":[{"sectionID":"48","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:48-10","research-permitext_discovered-id:52-7","research-permitext_discovered-id:3654-2","research-permitext_discovered-id:3659-1","research-permitext_discovered-id:6125-8","research-permitext_discovered-id:6199-4","research-permitext_discovered-id:4818-3","research-permitext_discovered-id:4880-6"],"relevance":"These selected 2022 NYC Building Code provisions concern specialized drawing content and do not govern DOB NOW PAA or Legalization workflow."}]}
